interface.longDescription:
Pathista runs the workflows you have written yourself, one step at a time, inside the chat.

A workflow is a graph of steps with the ways from one step to the next, loops included. Start a run and Pathista hands the assistant only the current step: the instructions you wrote for it and the edges that lead on. The position in the workflow, the variables, the notes and the history are kept in your Pathista account, so a run can be continued in a later message or a later chat.

What the assistant can do with it:
- list your workflows and start a run of one of them;
- read the current step and move along an edge once the step's work is done;
- set variables that an edge condition reads, keep notes and a todo list for the run;
- show the run as a graph with its progress;
- read, check, create and edit your workflows when you ask for it.

The step text is your own content, and only you can run your workflows. Pathista does not run generic to-do lists or reminders, and it does not run anyone else's workflows.

Sign in with your Pathista account when ChatGPT asks. Workflows and runs are managed on pathista.com.
